## Fields

Use structured fields. Do not dump the same fact in three places.

**Identity** — **Name**, **Acronym**, **Slug**, **Discipline** (specific profession: `vision rehabilitation`, `orthodontic technology`). Do not add a Sector option for a niche. **Sector**: prefer coarse tags already on the schema (`Health`, `Legal`, `Education`…). Existing niche tags may stay; do not grow the list. **Org type**, **Geography**, **Website**.

**Standing** — **Continuing education required**: Yes only when the gate is membership, register, or accreditation. Programme-only and statutory-only → No; still record hours in **CE requirement** (short fact, e.g. `250 hours / 5 years (UKCP)`). **Standing complexity**, **Public register**.

**Size and ops** — **Members estimate**, **Members band** (must match the estimate), **Count year** (calendar year of that estimate; empty if unpublished), **Established year**. **Admin model**, **Governance**, **Legal / charity no.** (`Co 09179719` or `Charity 1150137`). **Membership system** is the *class*; product name goes in **AMS product**. Wild Apricot uses class `MemberMojo / lightweight` — do not rename that option.

**Contacts** — **Primary email**, **Secondary email**, **Phone**, **Postal address**, **Named contact**, **Contact role**. **Contact notes**: leftovers only — never repeat emails, phones, or company numbers already in typed fields.

**Evidence** — **Sources**: URLs only, one per line or separated by ` ; `. **Tech signals**: one line. **Evidence confidence**: High = primary pages + a legal/register source; Medium = site only; Low = list mention or dead site. **Research status**: Stub (name only) | Researched (fields + short body) | Deepened (standing gate evidenced). **Last researched**: the day you checked.

**Pipeline** — Wave, component scores, **Score breakdown**, **Score notes**, **Send rank**. Do not write **Fit score**. **Outreach status**, **Survey status**, **Survey response summary** (Surveyor/Tally later). **Opted out** / **Opted out on** when they say stop. **Exclude reason**: one sentence so the next agent does not re-open the case.

**Marketing (every Core Active)**

- **ICP lane**: Core = Active **and** standing pain is likely still manual (volunteer or mix admin; manual / CMS / lightweight AMS; gated population is the membership or register product). Adjacent = Active but staffed mid-size, Known AMS, custom portal, or an accreditation track on a larger membership. Out = Backlog or Exclude. Active Wave + Adjacent lane is allowed — Wave is eligibility, lane is send priority.
- **Persona**: Secretary | Registrar | CEO / Director | Volunteer admin | Unknown
- **Lead source**: PSA register | HMRC List 3 | Peer of existing | Web search | Regulator site | Other
- **Next action**: Research | Draft survey email | Send survey | Follow up | Pause | Done
- **Campaign**: Survey wave 1 (sendable Core) | Later | Not queued
- **Outreach hook**: one sentence Mark can paste; no “CPD”
- **Pain hypothesis**: standing + fees + membership admin friction
- **Why now**: timing, not a second hook
- **Survey URL**: `https://research.goodstanding.co.uk/r/Bz5oLN?ref={slug}` for sendable Actives only
- **Preferred channel**, **Warmth** (Cold until they reply), **Owner** (Mark)
- **PSA accredited**, **Standing audit**, **Fee collection**, **Annual fee**, **Renewal month**
- **Member count source**, **Companies House URL**, **LinkedIn**, **Follow-up on**, **Last contacted**
- **Cluster**: PSA small register | Complementary | Animal | Celebrant / funeral | Land / conservation | Editing / finance | Counselling | Specialist health | Trade / guild | ADR / mediation | Other. Campaign batches, not another Sector tag.
- **Gated headcount**: people actually subject to the standing gate. Score **Size** from Members band; use gated headcount for Core vs Adjacent and an honest hook. Empty if unpublished.
- **Email quality**: Named person | Generic inbox | Unverified | None
- **CE policy URL** and **Register URL**: one-click evidence. **Sources** stays the full URL list.
- **Subject line**: must match `brand.mdc` (`A Short Survey`); no “CPD”
- **HQ town**: later in-person clustering

Do not put “CPD” in Outreach hook, Pain hypothesis, Why now, Subject line, or Score notes.

## Page body

Replace the whole body when cleaning a dumping-ground page. Do not append another spot-check heading.

```
## Purpose
One or two sentences.
## Establishment
Year, legal form, register status.
## Governance
Who runs it.
## Contacts
Only facts that are not already in properties, or a short named-person note.
## Website & systems
What the site is built on; whether CE is logged there.
## Fit notes
Wave + standing gate + why the score is what it is. One short deepen line if needed.
```

Never stack “spot-check — leave Exclude” sections. Update **Last researched** and **Exclude reason** instead.

## Research workflow

1. Follow this rule. Fetch the schema.
2. Search name, acronym, and slug before creating.
3. Read the body’s own membership, register, and continuing-education pages. Statutory regulator pages are supporting evidence, not a membership gate.
4. Fill structured fields first, then the short body.
5. Score into the component number fields. Set Wave from eligibility, not from the score. Do not write Fit score.
6. Unique slug. Recompute Send rank only if you can see the full sendable set; otherwise leave it empty.
7. Fetch the page you wrote: no duplicate emails in Contact notes; Sources are URLs; Score breakdown sums to Fit score; Stub has no Send rank.

## Parallel leftover hunting

Hunt in parallel, create in series. Two subagents must not create at the same time.

**Coordinator** owns Score audit, uniqueness lock, create, and reorient.

1. Query Score audit. If it is not empty, finish those Actives first. Do not launch hunters.
2. Partition remaining official lists into **disjoint** name batches. Typical slices: HMRC List 3 complementary leftovers; PSA complementary leftovers; Charity Commission / OSCR / CCNI healer-association leftovers; unpublished BAHA “40+” only if independently named with their own remaining-member hours.
3. Launch 2–4 hunter subagents in **one** turn. Each gets: this rule, data source `9952bb13-ed3e-4c1f-8df5-6f65b98c4323`, sit-on / already-slugged names **for its slice only**, and **do not create / do not update CRM rows**.
4. Merge packets. Drop already-slugged, sit-on, individuals, universities, Republic of Ireland-only, and statutory-only leftovers.
5. Uniqueness-search the remaining names again.
6. Create **2–3 unique slugs** only (coordinator, or one creator). `allow_async: true`, then poll. Re-query Score audit until empty. Recritical Fit / Wave / lane. Add a CRM field only if a real hole appears. Do not invent Send ranks. Campaign = Not queued on leftover creates.
7. Repeat until remaining official lists are exhausted.

Coordinator replies stay short. Evidence lives in hunter packets and on CRM pages.

**Hunters** (read-only): uniqueness-search each name; read membership / register / standing pages; return a packet; stop. Must not create, update, or invent Send ranks.

Packet — one line per name, plus a short Unique block only when needed:

- **Already slugged** — exact title + page id
- **Sit-on** — leftover name → existing slug
- **Do not slug** — individual, university, venue, church-without-gate, statutory, no remaining-member body
- **Needs coordinator fetch** — search ambiguous; do not mark Unique
- **Unique, ready** — kebab slug; standing gate; Wave / ICP lane; Fit as `standing/size/systems/admin/contact`; official inbox or none; 3–8 source URLs; Distinct from…; Do not copy… (named-person / shared umbrella inboxes)

Absorbed / amalgamated / dissolved names still on an official list: return **Unique, ready** as Exclude even if search is empty.

**Creator** (one at a time): receives only coordinator-rechecked Unique, ready packets. Creates those 2–3 rows. Does not hunt. Score checked = true. Last researched = today. Send rank empty. Coordinator re-proves Score audit.

